      {
        "id": 200995,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-04T20:00:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mwc146\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n mwc146:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That's possible. If that's the case, I hope that there's a way to quickly cycle through the missions, so you don't get stuck for a while with a set that applies to heroes that aren't around.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>What do you mean by \"applies to heroes that aren't around\"? &nbsp;It looks to me like every mission will be completable by any hero, and the reward will be useful to almost any hero. &nbsp;Sure, some will be easier and/or more beneficial for specific heroes, but most of the missions we've seen look pretty easy to achieve under most circumstances.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>To Hope For the Dawn will be tricky for Mr. Fixer or The Sentinels, but even that isn't impossible since they can earn power-granting cards like The Infinity Cannon, or the Rod of Anubis.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:29:24.727Z",
