      {
        "id": 200997,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-04T21:47:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>That's... probably not going to do nearly as much as you'd like. &nbsp;Unless the targets are much, much tougher than any we've seen before, the first wave or two will wipe out all the minor targets, and then there won't be any left for Mr. Fixer to turn into AOE damage. &nbsp;Which is still a ton of damage. &nbsp;But not 9*X to each target where X is the number of non-hero targets. &nbsp;Probably more like 27 damage to each target.</p><p>A better option would probably be Dual Crowbars. &nbsp;Sure, they won't do as much damage overall, but you can pile the additional damage all on OblivAeon.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Assuming that OblivAeon is a damage sponge like Akash'buta rather than having some sort of damage immunity, of course.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:29:24.851Z",
